      ":question/id": "3ab78de4-fd92-5b9f-a2b2-9f7ec02329f0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $12\\times 12$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=10,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=12.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+10 & =12 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
